        "message": "Deliver patch-2 (workspace v6) for the hexbin mincnt/C inconsistency.\n\nChange: in lib/matplotlib/axes/_axes.py Axes.hexbin, the C-given branch used\n`reduce_C_function(acc) if len(acc) > mincnt else np.nan`, which required\nstrictly more than mincnt points per hexagon. The C-is-None branch uses\n`accum[accum < mincnt] = np.nan`, i.e. at least mincnt points. Changed the\nC-given comparison to `len(acc) >= mincnt`, exactly the Resolution requested\nin the issue (`len(vals) >= mincnt` rather than `len(vals) > mincnt`).\n\nTest evidence on this exact version: public lib/matplotlib/tests/test_axes.py\n-k hexbin -> 7 collected, 7 passed, 0 failed, 0 errors (report\ntest-report-7c765d86ede677a574f4ed6c). A focused issue reproduction (since\nremoved; workspace is back to only the one-file source change, diff_sha256\n4ae15aa9...) also confirmed hexagon counts are identical with and without C\nfor mincnt in {1,2,3} and that single-datum hexagons are retained.\n\nNote: the existing public hexbin tests do not mention mincnt at all, so they\nestablish no regression rather than direct coverage; the focused reproduction\nwas what actually exercised the changed branch. Hidden acceptance is not\nverified by these runs.",
